<%- include("partials/header.ejs") %>

<div class="api-page">

    <section class="api-hero">
        <span class="api-label">API &amp; DATA</span>
        <h1>How Sonara<br>gets its music data.</h1>
        <p> Sonara uses Apple's iTunes Search API to search for and
            retrieve music information used throughout the website.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>01</span>
            <h2>Data source</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-content">
            <p> Sonara uses the iTunes Search API provided by Apple
                to retrieve information about artists, albums, songs,
                genres, and other music content.
            </p>
            <p> The API allows Sonara to search Apple's available music
                catalog and use the returned information to create
                the music discovery experience on the website.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="api-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>02</span>
            <h2>What Sonara uses</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="data-grid">
            <article class="data-card">
                <span class="data-number">01</span>
                <h3>Artists</h3>
                <p> Artist names and information used to help users
                    discover and explore artists.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="data-card">
                <span class="data-number">02</span>
                <h3>Albums</h3>
                <p> Album names, artwork, release information, and
                    related music data.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="data-card">
                <span class="data-number">03</span>
                <h3>Songs</h3>
                <p> Track names, artists, albums, and available
                    promotional previews.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="data-card">
                <span class="data-number">04</span>
                <h3>Genres</h3>
                <p> Genre information used to organize and explore
                    different types of music.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="data-card">
                <span class="data-number">05</span>
                <h3>Artwork</h3>
                <p> Album artwork made available through the music
                    catalog data.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="data-card">
                <span class="data-number">06</span>
                <h3>Previews</h3>
                <p> Short music previews made available for
                    promotional music discovery.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="api-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>03</span>
            <h2>Searching</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-content">
            <p> When you search for music on Sonara, your search is
                processed and the relevant information is retrieved
                from the iTunes Search API.
            </p>
            <p> Search results can include artists, albums, songs,
                and other music-related information depending on
                the type of search being performed.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="api-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>04</span>
            <h2>Example request</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block">
            <div class="code-header">
                <span>iTunes Search API</span>
            </div>
            <pre><code>https://itunes.apple.com/search?term=daft%20punk&amp;entity=song</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p class="code-description">
            This is an example of the type of request that can be
            made to search the iTunes music catalog.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-section legal-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>05</span>
            <h2>Attribution &amp; usage</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-content">
            <p> Sonara uses promotional content made available through
                Apple's iTunes Search API for music discovery and
                promotional purposes.
            </p>
            <p> Song previews are provided courtesy of iTunes and are
                intended to allow users to discover the associated
                music.
            </p>
            <p class="legal-note">
                Apple, iTunes, and related trademarks belong to Apple Inc.
                Sonara is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed
                by Apple.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

</div>

<%- include("partials/footer.ejs") %>